# The validator of an array or a tuple reads elements only from a plain array. An array with holes, accessors or names of its own and a proxy of an array are left to the general validator, which reads each element once: the validator calls nothing that could run an iterator, a getter or a trap
# FORM: Prepared optimizing
# RUN: derived-functions Validator:x0.0 Validator:x1.0
# STATISTIC: ValidatorsCreated = 2

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
expectedresult x0 type=Array<number> validation=[{shape=Array{element=1} type=Array<number>}, {shape=Primitive{primitive=Number} type=number}]
expectedresult x1 type=Array validation=[{shape=Tuple{elements=[1, 1] required=2} type=Array}, {shape=Primitive{primitive=Number} type=number}]

